ce, brown rice, porridge, and timer settings are useful. A long menu list is less important than rice consistency, keep-warm quality, cleaning, and reliability.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>What makes a rice cooker frustrating over time?</summary><p class="faq-answer">Common frustrations include rice drying out on warm, a scratched inner pot, confusing controls, poor small-batch results, and lids or steam vents that are annoying to clean.</p></details>
